  "parentCard": {
    "title": "The rhyme walk",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "why-walk",
    "steps": [
      "Step outside together and open the game: what rhymes with tree? Bee, knee, see, or a made-up word; anything whose ending sings the same counts.",
      "Take turns hunting rhymes for things you pass: sky, stone, sun. One real word or one silly word each, and the sillier the better.",
      "Ask one why question about a find and wonder about it together: why does tree rhyme with bee when they look nothing alike? Where does the rhyme live, in the thing or in the word?",
      "On the way home, rhyme their own name into something silly and let them giggle. Sounds are toys today."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Do they hear a rhyme in their ear, or do they need the two words said side by side first?",
      "Do they offer made-up rhyme words on their own? Made-up words are a win here, not a mistake.",
      "Which do they enjoy more: finding a real rhyme or inventing a silly one?"
    ]
  }
